    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c871ae4b_af50b52e",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-03T18:04:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t looked at the trng init/exit code, but in derive_pos_match_secret you wrap the rand_bytes with that. Does that need to be done here? If we need to call it every time maybe wrap it in a helper function. Otherwise, if we only need to init once maybe we just do it at the beginning of fp_sensor_task.",
      "revId": "78c707552d70f0b054337d71937d7f3636c91e3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10a079f8_ab9210aa",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-03T19:01:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To use trng\u0027s random functions you have to call init_trng/exit_trng, otherwise you get runtime error. You can\u0027t call it once at the beginning and leave it on because that wastes power: https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/include/trng.h?q\u003dtrng+file:%5Esrc/platform/ec/+package:%5Echromeos_public$\u0026g\u003d0\u0026l\u003d23\n\nIn derive_pos_match_secret I am wrapping both rand_bytes and rand_finger_id, so here I am already in trng context.\n\nI would prefer the current way of wrapping, because if you use a helper function to init/exit trng, when you want to execute rand_bytes multiple times at once like here (first new_pos_match_salt then finger_id) you are shutting down hardware trng then immediately reopening it, which makes me uncomfortable.",
      "parentUuid": "c871ae4b_af50b52e",
      "revId": "78c707552d70f0b054337d71937d7f3636c91e3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
